+
+# 2026-11-25-composer-message-source
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-25-composer-message-source.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Recognize the released input-prediction message source when generating composer suggestions.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-25-composer-message-source
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:agent/inbox/spliced"
+    previous: "2026-11-24-z-released-memory-usage"
+    after: "2fb98b5146e063e8c4b855547d2fb27092c9040726cbac89aa3a465716f57a21"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:developer/message"
+    previous: "2026-11-24-z-released-memory-usage"
+    after: "92b48a4462b836a9ade29713dc2d75bf15741291dcec92ea53ced7ab06738ffd"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:memory/extraction"
+    previous: "2026-11-24-z-released-memory-usage"
+    after: "d46f5d2bf654beb8638f86e1260bbb0983ccfbc96124ac1e894d392694046f41"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:session/title-llm-request"
+    previous: "2026-11-24-z-released-memory-usage"
+    after: "54e74922e03ad8ec356b23a16400d179b88208e493a81a0e2af7cdc98277b0e6"
+    decision: same-version
+  - root: "event:user/message"
+    previous: "2026-11-24-z-released-memory-usage"
+    after: "110e5a2ec55ee0f1b7aaf9fa96559512b5a21bf3460f26e06458c93198081137"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Both DSHU releases 2026.11.23.0 and 2026.11.24.3 write this source inside a v4 input/prediction request. The candidate uses the same notice source and the same request and result fields. It can read existing records with or without an optional request. The older DSHU reader can read the new records under its original discriminator. The prediction producer appends neither a chat message nor an inbox entry. The wider shared source type also appears in the declared user, developer, inbox, memory and title types. Their writers and stored fields are unchanged.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The Host prediction test compares normalized events against the request and result produced by the released writer. The Chromium composer test used the real Host with a recorded model, kept Tab local and retained the opt-out after reload.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
