+# 2026-11-26-released-protection-audits
+
+English | [中文](2026-11-26-released-protection-audits.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Recognizes protection audit entries in released DSHU v4 conversations, including entries that retain fingerprints without readable identities.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Declaration](#declaration)
+- [Compatibility](#compatibility)
+- [Verification](#verification)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+<a id="declaration"></a>
+## Declaration
+
+```yaml persistence-change
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: 2026-11-26-released-protection-audits
+baseline: false
+changes:
+  - root: "event:target/admission"
+    previous: null
+    after: "8c3913646d7d1cce13d34dc0cd98f0ca98e230acecdcdfe7fb120f927d2f7165"
+    decision: same-version
+```
+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+The two DSHU releases write target/admission with no surface operation. The reader preserves the entry, including omitted or null fields, in its original sequence. Replay derives no message, authorization or action from the recorded decision. The candidate adds no producer. Existing v4 readers see exactly the audit data the original writer committed when they reopen the log.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+The JSONL current-event-admission suite reopens a fingerprint-only entry after appending and checks its original bytes. The release-data fixture uses each released audit store and Session writer to create plain and compressed logs, then checks the historical events and projected conversation when continuing and after restarting.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+## Dev Note
+
+None.
