+# Cross-conversation memory
+
+English | [中文](memory.zh.md)
+
+The standard and writing presets can recall saved preferences, project facts, operation results and writing settings on relevant turns. Users enable memory in General settings and opt into automatic extraction separately. Both preferences default to off.
+
+## Storage and session history
+
+The [memory service](../../packages/memory/memory/README.md) stores records in the user data directory. A session appends the versions and text it actually used. Editing, disabling or deleting a record affects future retrieval. On resume the session projection reads the log to identify versions already injected.
+
+## Management and cost
+
+The [settings page](../../packages/client/ui-settings-memory/README.md) uses the [management API](../../packages/api/memory-controller/README.md) to list, edit and delete records. Existing records remain manageable while memory is off. Automatic extraction makes a separate model request after a successful turn. Spending admission applies and available usage contributes to the session estimate. Its request and outcome are logged in the source session.
+
+<!-- BEGIN GENERATED cordis-surface (gen-cordis-catalog.ts) — do not edit between markers -->
+
+<a id="cordis-surface"></a>
+
+## Cordis API
+
