@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+---
+description: "Owner access to scoped memory management and extraction preferences."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-api-memory-controller
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+The management panel uses `ctx.remote.memory` to read, edit and delete saved records. Changes check the record or settings version. Only the application owner can manage memory across workspaces. Retrieval by a running conversation follows its own scope.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Management methods](#management)
+- [Errors](#errors)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="management"></a>
+## Management methods
+
+- `describe()` returns the active retrieval limits, registered workspaces and mode IDs present in saved records.
+- `configure(request)` changes the master switch or automatic extraction after checking the settings revision. Turning either off cancels active extraction.
+- `configureExtraction(request)` updates the extraction preference with the same revision check.
+- `retryExtraction(sessionId)` retries extraction for an open, idle session and returns its latest status.
+- `list(request)` filters by scope, type, status and text, sorts by most recent edit and checks the source session. A failed lookup returns `unknown` and leaves the record intact. This is also the status when no persistence service can check the source.
+- `create(request)` saves a confirmed record attributed to the user of the management panel.
+- `update(request)` checks `expectedVersion`. On `memory/conflict` the client retains the draft for review and retry.
+- `setStatus(request)` checks the version before enabling or disabling a record.
+- `deleteRecord(request)` permanently deletes a record and reports whether it existed. The service uses `remove`, a reserved name on the Remote interface.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="errors"></a>
+## Errors
+
+`memory/conflict` provides the record ID and both versions. `memory/not-found` identifies the missing record. `memory/invalid` and `memory/unavailable` include a reason. Other callers receive `remote-access/denied`.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+Indirectly, through edits that the memory service uses when selecting records for subsequent turns.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Management requests use the Host API. A changed record can contribute new text to a later model request.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The API manages individual records. Bulk transfers and revision browsing are unavailable.
+- Deletion removes the record from future retrieval. Earlier session logs retain their recorded text. There are no tombstones.
+- The application composes the panel through `api/remotes`. This package supplies the Host methods.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance reference</summary>
+
+See the [memory service](../../memory/memory/README.md) for storage, retrieval and lifecycle rules.
+
+</details>
