 ## Summary
 
-`dsh-client-ui-theme` lets Web GUI users choose `light`, `dark`, or `system`, and set the font and font size of text, code, and the terminal separately in Settings. Every authenticated browser stores these values in the `ui-theme` settings namespace, which the local provider persists in `$DSH_HOME/cordis.patch.yml` by default. The plugin resolves `system` through `prefers-color-scheme` and publishes immutable `ThemeSnapshot`s; ui-layout applies each snapshot to the document. The package also ships the `--dsw-*` token stylesheets and injects a synchronous bootstrap so the selected palette, font size, and fonts apply before the shell loads. Third-party themes can register alias-token overrides through `ctx.theme`.
+The default theme switches between light and dark at local sunrise and sunset. In General settings, choose a city, follow the system palette, or keep a fixed light or dark theme. Text, code, and terminal fonts and sizes can be set independently. Saved preferences apply before the shell appears on the next launch.
 
 ## Table of Contents
 
@@ -25,18 +25,20 @@ English | [中文](README.zh.md)
 <a id="use-this-package"></a>
 ## Use this package
 
+The sunrise/sunset location selector uses the shared application menu. Running-reasoning text, its whale icon and shimmer follow the current mode accent in both light and dark themes.
+
 Users switch the color scheme, font sizes, and fonts from rows in Settings (General section); the choices persist across restarts in every authenticated browser. Feature plugins consume the current snapshot through `ctx.theme` and read the `--dsw-*` tokens in CSS; they do not manage theme state themselves.
 
 ### Appearance and font size
 
-In narrow browser settings, the three Appearance choices share one row and font-size labels use a smaller gutter. At viewport widths up to 767 CSS px, including narrow desktop windows, font-family rows stack each title, description, and full-width field vertically. Font-size steppers stay to the right of their labels. Wider viewports retain horizontal font-family rows. Windows and macOS desktop windows retain wrapping Appearance choices and standard font-size label spacing. Font-family fields use 16 px text on devices with a coarse primary pointer.
