+---
+description: "Account balances and account-specific local samples for the sidebar and quota settings."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-balance
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Web and Desktop display the grant balance, topped-up balance and local history. The service prefers the signed-in account and otherwise uses the configured API key. The UI receives balance data without credentials.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Sampling and retention](#sampling)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="sampling"></a>
+## Sampling and retention
+
+The default refresh interval is 15 seconds. Choose an integer from 3 to 3600 seconds. Sampling and sidebar visibility have separate switches. The public API returns the current balance, so the curve begins with the first local sample.
+
+Saving a sample cleans up records older than 30 days by default. Existing choices to disable cleanup or retain a sample count take precedence. Quota settings read the full retained history. The sidebar starts with a seven-day view and also offers one or 30 days, ending at the most recent sample. For a limited response it keeps both endpoints, prioritizes recent balance increases and fills the remaining positions across the range. On-disk samples retain their timestamps and original precision.
+
+Manual cleanup applies to the account history shown in settings. If the account changes before confirmation or while cleanup waits for an earlier sample, review the refreshed history and confirm your selection. A write already submitted for the previous account can finish only in that account’s history.
+
+The read result carries a `historyTag` for that account history on this Host. Pass it as `expectedHistory` to `clear`. The response sets `cleanupApplied` to true when the write commits, including if the account changes during the write. A changed identity receives an empty sample list.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as account balance samples appear only in the user interface.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Checking a balance does not call a model or change a conversation prefix.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The chart begins with the first saved sample. Switching API keys selects another history. Switching back restores the previous history.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance reference</summary>
+
+The Host owns account selection and writes. Settings and the sidebar read the same retained samples.
+
+</details>
