+---
+description: "Bundled fiction manuals and reference sheets for Writing sessions."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# Writing playbooks
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Writing sessions can load seven fiction manuals by name. Five include reference sheets for working on drafts, scenes, style, continuity and long-form structure. The [Writing preset](../../bundle/web-app/presets/writing.patch.yml) supplies the catalog and the `skill` tool.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Configuration](#configuration)
+- [Model experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known limitations and deferred work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+
+<a id="configuration"></a>
+
+## Configuration
+
+The preset registers `dsh-playbooks` with `packs: [writing]`. An empty pack list registers no provider. To relocate the files, set `assetRoot` to an absolute directory containing the [writing pack](assets/writing). Each manual's directory resolves its relative reference paths. Missing pack directories, empty packs and unreadable or malformed catalog files fail plugin activation.
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Writing manuals
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The session's skill catalog advertises each manual's name and description. Calling `skill` with the name loads its body and reference directory. Users may also invoke a manual by name.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Catalog entries consume input tokens when the catalog is delivered. Only the selected manual's body enters the conversation on invocation.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+The skill catalog and loaded manual are appended to session history. Later requests retain the preceding message prefix.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- Reference sheets are separate Markdown files. Reading a sheet requires access to its file in the manual's resource directory.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Maintenance notes</summary>
+
+The seven manual names and their relative reference paths are shared with released Writing sessions.
+
+</details>
