+# Story bible skeleton
+
+Copy this into `story/bible/` and fill it in. Keep entries short; the bible is a working document, not an encyclopedia.
+
+## premise.md
+
+```markdown
+# Premise
+One paragraph: who wants what, what stands in the way, what happens if they fail.
+
+# Theme
+The question the story asks. The lie the protagonist believes. The truth they resist.
+
+# Genre promises
+What the reader is here for (dread, catharsis, romance, puzzle, awe). What the story will never do.
+
+# Tone
+Three adjectives and one comparable work. What the prose sounds like on a good page.
+
+# Ending
+The intended final image, even if the path is open.
+```
+
+## characters.md
+
+```markdown
+## NAME
+- Role:
+- Age / appearance:
+- Want:
+- Need:
+- Wound:
+- Voice:
+- Habits and tells:
+- Relationships:
+- Arc:
+- Secrets:
+- First appearance:
+```
+
+## world.md
+
+```markdown
+## Rules
+What is possible, what it costs, who controls it.
+
+## Geography
+Places that matter, distances, travel time, climate.
+
+## Institutions
+Power structures, laws, money, religion, technology level.
+
+## Daily life
+Food, work, clothing, slang, rituals. Three concrete details per category.
+```
+
+## timeline.md
+
+```markdown
+| Day | Event | Characters | Consequence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 1 |  |  |  |
+```
+
+## canon.md
+
+```markdown
+# Hard facts
+- Names, ages, deaths, marriages, physical rules.
+
+# Author decisions
+- YYYY-MM-DD: user changed X to Y; earlier references updated in chapters N–M.
+
+# Promises to the reader
+- Planted clues that must pay off.
+```
+
+## style.md
+
+```markdown
+- POV:
+- Tense:
+- Dialogue format:
+- Scene break marker:
+- Spelling variant:
+- Chapter length target:
+- Explicit-content level:
+```
+
+## threads.md
+
+```markdown
+| ID | Thread | Planted in | Status | Payoff target |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| T1 |  | ch01 | open | ch12 |
+```
